A||||5||mwbackus||Coil Overs||||1||
Z||000000||mwbackus||03-04-2000||11:21 PM||||Is anyone using the rear coil over setup from Ground Effects:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ground-control.com/default.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ground-control.com/default.htm</A> <P>They are only $200 and use the existing strut without grinding off the spring seats like the Ryane assemblies entail.  <P>I am planning to purchase a set, and would appreciate any opinions.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-05-2000||01:12 AM||||Wish they had a set for the front.  Looks like an easy adjustment.  Let us know how things turn out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||03-05-2000||02:09 AM||||Mike, don't you have an 88? I didn't see one made for 88's. These 88's are a curse sometimes... no parts or they cost a butt load.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||03-05-2000||02:57 AM||||Nice thing about the 88 rear strut assembly is that it is almost the same as earlier years.  You can even use the rear lowering springs designed for pre 88's.  The lower strut mount is just slightly different, and  requires a very small amount of grinding to get a precise fit of the pre-88 strut design.<P><BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||03-05-2000||11:41 AM||||Thanks mwbackus, I am looking into lowering my 86 and was asking about this in another post. This sounds like a good was to do the rear, not a bad price. I'm going to look into them also. Let me know if you get them soon.<BR>Are you lowering the front? what springs are you going with?<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||03-05-2000||02:27 PM||||I already got the new KYB's and poly for the rear.  It occured to me that by using the coil over assembly, one would not even have to mess with spring removal /install (ie.. spring compressor).  The front end is a different story.  I am still looking for an economical method of lowering the front without a total mess up of the geometry.  <P>GM used to sell modified control arms for the 88 to be used with lowering springs.  Dont know how much or if they are still available.  <BR>The only option for drop spindles for the 88 I have found are from Ryane. Perhaps they will drop the prices down now that the pre-88 spindles are so cheaply obtained from carparts.com, and everyone knows how badly they have been ripping us off.<P>Has anyone used the RCC products on the 88 front?<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
